      "review": "Correct only the Decoding Acceleration and Serving Systems paragraph, keeping other content and all source URLs/provenance. Fetch https://arxiv.org/html/2211.17192 section 2.1 to verify the algorithm.\n\nThe draft/approximation model generates a candidate token sequence autoregressively; the large target model evaluates those candidate positions in parallel. The current sentence incorrectly says the lightweight draft generates its candidates in parallel. Rewrite it accurately and cite [20][12]. Explain acceptance/rejection or exact target-distribution preservation briefly, without claiming exactness for sparse approximations [21].\n\nAlso narrow the opening universal claim that autoregressive generation inherently suffers from memory bandwidth starvation: decoding can be memory-bandwidth limited depending on batch size/hardware, not all workloads. Keep it supported by the speculative decoding primary paper. Do not invent measured speedups. Submit the complete corrected body and rerun checks inside sandbox.\n",
      "before_report_sha256": "e439a6d3ba442ba8821072f45c683725d3e339c29a1a334f9a4fc33b1ad49da2"
